signed. A host accepts only a list whose sequence is above the one it holds, which is what stops a host, a relayer or an attacker holding an old list from rolling the room\'s withdrawals back."},"issuedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the room signed this list."},"entries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4096,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RevocationEntry"},"description":"Every withdrawal still in force, in the order the room made them. Empty is valid: a room that has revoked nothing, or whose every entry has lapsed, can still state its sequence."},"proof":{"type":"object","description":"The room\'s Data Integrity proof over every other member, made with a key the room\'s DID document lists for `assertionMethod`."}}},"RevocationEntry":{"title":"RevocationEntry","description":"One withdrawal in a `RevocationList`, discriminated by `kind`.\\n\\n  - `credential` withdraws one credential, named by its `id`. It matches the membership credential or any authority link whose `id` equals `credentialId`.\\n  - `subject` withdraws a party: every credential the room\'s chain gave them **before** `revokedAt`. It matches the membership credential or any authority link whose `credentialSubject` id **or** `issuer` is `subject` and whose `validFrom` is earlier than `revokedAt`. Matching the issuer as well as the subject withdraws what the party delegated before their removal, which no re-admission revives. A credential carrying no `validFrom` is treated as issued before every entry.\\n  - `room` withdraws every credential whose `validFrom` is earlier than `revokedAt`, whoever holds it. It is how a room resets access — after a compromise, or on a `private` room, where naming a party would disclose who was a member.\\n\\n**Keyed on time, so a party can come back.** A `subject` or `room` entry withdraws what was issued before it and nothing after, so a room that re-admits a removed party issues fresh credentials and they verify. A `credential` entry is permanent for that one credential, which nobody re-issues.\\n\\n**Tiers.** On a `private` room a host MUST refuse a list carrying a `credential` or `subject` entry: a presentation there withholds the credential and its subject, so such an entry is one the host cannot apply and a disclosure of who was in the room. Only `room` entries are permitted, and a host serving a `private` room MUST refuse any presentation for which it cannot establish that no credential in it has a `validFrom` earlier than the latest `room` entry\'s `revokedAt`.","oneOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/CredentialRevocation"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/SubjectRevocation"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RoomRevocation"}]},"RoomRevocation":{"title":"RoomRevocation","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","revokedAt"],"description":"Withdraws every credential whose `validFrom` is earlier than `revokedAt`, whoever holds it.","properties":{"kind":{"const":"room"},"revokedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the room made this withdrawal."},"until":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"OPTIONAL. After this instant every credential the entry matches has expired anyway, so a host MAY discard the entry and the room MAY omit it from later lists. Absent means the entry is kept for as long as the room keeps a list."}}},"SubjectRevocation":{"title":"SubjectRevocation","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","subject","revokedAt"],"description":"Withdraws a party: every credential naming them as subject or issuer whose `validFrom` is earlier than `revokedAt`.","properties":{"kind":{"const":"subject"},"subject":{"type":"string","pattern":"^did:","maxLength":2048,"description":"The party withdrawn. Never the room itself."},"revokedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the room made this withdrawal."},"until":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"OPTIONAL. After this instant every credential the entry matches has expired anyway, so a host MAY discard the entry and the room MAY omit it from later lists. Absent means the entry is kept for as long as the room keeps a list."}}},"CredentialRevocation":{"title":"CredentialRevocation","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","credentialId","revokedAt"],"description":"Withdraws one credential — a membership credential or any authority link — by its `id`.","properties":{"kind":{"const":"credential"},"credentialId":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The `id` of the credential withdrawn, as `rooms/owner/issue-authority` and `rooms/owner/issue-membership` return it, or as an attenuated credential carries it."},"revokedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the room made this withdrawal."},"until":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"OPTIONAL. After this instant every credential the entry matches has expired anyway, so a host MAY discard the entry and the room MAY omit it from later lists. Absent means the entry is kept for as long as the room keeps a list."}}},"AuthorityPresentation":{"title":"AuthorityPresentation","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["membership","authority"],"description":"What a party presents to act on a room. Carries the whole authority chain: a host MUST NOT dereference an authority credential\'s `parent` to fetch a link it was not given. Resolving over the network would make verification depend on availability, turn every identifier into a request the host can be induced to make against an address the holder chooses, and signal credential use to whoever hosts the identifier. A host MUST bind the presenter to the chain\'s leaf. A chain that verifies is evidence that authority was conferred on somebody; it is not evidence that the party presenting it is that somebody. The leaf\'s subject MUST equal the party the host authenticated for this request — an identity the transport established or a document `proof` proved, never one named in a payload. A host that omits this check authorizes every captured presentation, and the omission is silent, because the chain still verifies.\\n\\n**Every credential is its issuer\'s attestation, and only its issuer\'s.** For the membership credential and for every link of `authority`, a host MUST verify the credential\'s `proof` with a key that the credential\'s own `issuer` lists for `assertionMethod` in its DID document, and MUST refuse a credential whose proof names a verification method that is not its issuer\'s. A proof that verifies under some other party\'s key is that party\'s statement, not the issuer\'s, and confers nothing. The same binding holds for every other document a room signs, such as a `RevocationList`.\\n\\n**A chain that verifies may still be revoked.** A host that has accepted a `RevocationList` for the room (`rooms/revocations/put`) MUST, from the moment it accepted it, refuse every presentation in which the membership credential or any link of `authority` is revoked by that list, under every task and every version of every task it serves for the room. A chain from which any link is revoked is refused whole: a credential delegated from a revoked one confers nothing, however it was attenuated. The refusal is the same `permissionDenied` as any other failed presentation.","properties":{"membership":{"type":"string","description":"The presenter\'s membership credential for this room, or — on a `private` room — a zero-knowledge presentation of it. Serialized per the governing profile."},"authority":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":8,"items":{"type":"string"},"description":"The authority chain, LEAF FIRST: the first element is the credential being relied on and the last MUST be one issued by the room itself. Every link the presenter relies on is present, because the host will not fetch one. Capped at 8: verification is linear in chain length and runs on every operation, so an unbounded chain is a denial-of-service surface against the host. The known uses need 2 to 3 — a person attenuating to an agent, and that agent to a sub-agent."},"subjectBinding":{"type":"string","description":"REQUIRED on a `private` room, where the subject identifier is withheld: a proof that the membership credential and the authority chain\'s leaf describe the SAME subject. Without it two parties pool credentials — one contributes membership, the other authority — and the combination verifies as a single party holding both. A host MUST refuse a private-room presentation that omits this."}}}}}';

